Conclusion:
The cardiotocographic dataset was successfully analyzed using various exploratory data analysis techniques. Missing values were handled using mean imputation to maintain data consistency, and descriptive statistics helped summarize the distribution and variability of the features. Histograms and violin plots showed that most variables had uneven distributions with variations in spread, while boxplots revealed the presence of several outliers. These outliers were treated using the IQR method by capping extreme values, which improved data stability without removing records. The correlation heatmap indicated both positive and negative relationships among certain features, suggesting that some variables are moderately related and may influence each other. Scatter plots and pair plots further highlighted patterns, trends, and variability between selected features such as LB, AC, FM, and UC. The analysis also showed that the dataset contains some fluctuations and variability across measurements, which is common in medical datasets. Overall, the dataset has been effectively cleaned, analyzed, and visualized, making it suitable for further machine learning and predictive analysis tasks.